@* Sales.razor — Phase 4.2

   Customer-facing order history page at route `/Sales`. ALL authenticated
   users land here (the sidebar link in MainLayout.razor is wrapped in a
   bare <AuthorizeView>). The backend handler enforces role-based scoping:
     - Admin / Manager / Employee / ReadOnly: see ALL sales in the system
       (the "staff audit view").
     - Customer: see only their own sales (the "my orders" view).

   BACKEND CONTRACT:
     - Load: GetSalesPaginatedQuery(PageNumber, PageSize, SearchTerm?)
       → PaginatedResult<SaleListItemDto>
       - The handler resolves the current user from ICurrentUserService
         server-side, so callers CANNOT snoop on other users' sales by
         passing a foreign id.
       - Search term matches SaleNumber OR CustomerName (case-insensitive,
         applied in-memory on the loaded page — see handler comment).
       - The spec always orders by CreatedAtUtc DESC, so the newest sale
         appears first on page 1. After /Cart's Submit navigates here,
         the just-submitted sale is at the top of the list.
     - Click a row's sale number or View button → /Sales/{Id}. The detail
       page (Phase 4.3 — not yet built) will load GetSaleByIdQuery. The
       route is reserved here so the URL is meaningful even when 4.3 404s.

   LAYOUT:
     1. Page header: title + "Continue shopping" button → /Products.
     2. Filter bar: search box + status filter dropdown.
     3. Sales table: RadzenDataGrid (no built-in pager) with columns for
        sale number (link), status (color-coded badge), total, customer
        name (staff-only), created-by name (staff-only), created-at, and
        an actions column with a View button.
     4. Manual pager below the table (Prev / page numbers / Next + total
        count). Same pattern as Products.razor and AdminProducts.razor.
     5. Empty state with a "Submit a cart to create your first order"
        hint and a Go to cart button.

   DATA LOADING:
     - OnInitializedAsync: load the first page of sales.
     - On search/page/status-filter change: re-call GetSalesPaginatedQuery
       via Wolverine. Search is debounced via RadzenTextBox's
       bind-Value:after (fires on Enter or blur, not every keystroke —
       same approach as Products.razor). The status filter and page
       changes also reload from the backend.
     - Status filter is SERVER-SIDE (Phase 7 item E). The query accepts an
       optional SaleStatus? that is pushed down into the spec → SQL WHERE
       clause, so TotalCount is accurate and the filter scales beyond one
       page. Previously this was client-side on the materialized page,
       which broke pagination for staff with many sales.

   ROLE-GATED COLUMNS:
     - Customer / non-staff users see only: Sale number, Status, Total,
       Created At, Actions. The "Customer" and "Created By" columns are
       noise for them (Customer = themselves on every row; Created By is
       an audit detail).
     - Staff (Admin/Manager/Employee/ReadOnly) see all columns including
       Customer (who the sale is for) and Created By (who keyed it in).
       Hiding these for staff would hide useful audit info; showing them
       to customers leaks nothing they don't already know but is noise.

   ANTIFORGERY:
     Not needed — no EditForm. All button clicks are sync navigations or
     async event handlers that dispatch queries via Wolverine. The Blazor
     circuit's anti-forgery token is established at circuit start. *@

@page "/Sales"
@attribute [Authorize]
@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Authorization
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.Queries.GetSalesPaginated
@using TakOne.Domain.Sales.Enums
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.DTOs
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<Sales> Loc

<PageTitle>@Loc["PageTitle"]</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
        /* Sale number — monospace + primary color so it reads as a clickable
           identifier. The link itself is the clickable element; the wrapper
           just provides consistent typography. */
        .sale-number-link {
            font-family: var(--rz-monospace-font-family, ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace);
            font-weight: 600;
            color: var(--rz-primary);
            text-decoration: none;
        }

        .sale-number-link:hover {
            text-decoration: underline;
        }

        /* Status badge — RadzenBadge with BadgeStyle handles colors; this
           just normalizes the width so badges in a column line up. */
        .sale-status-badge {
            min-width: 96px;
            display: inline-flex;
            justify-content: center;
        }

        /* Total — right-aligned tabular numbers so columns line up. */
        .sale-total {
            font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        /* Muted timestamp for the "Created At" column. The timestamp is
           secondary info; the sale number is the primary identifier. */
        .sale-timestamp {
            color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
            font-size: 0.9rem;
        }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Page header ──
       Title + "Continue shopping" button. The button is always visible
       (any user browsing their orders might want to go back to shopping). *@
    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal"
                 AlignItems="AlignItems.Center"
                 JustifyContent="JustifyContent.SpaceBetween"
                 Wrap="FlexWrap.Wrap"
                 Gap="0.75rem">
        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
            <RadzenIcon Icon="receipt_long" Style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--rz-primary);" />
            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["PageHeading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
        </RadzenStack>

        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ContinueShoppingButton"]"
                      Icon="storefront"
                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                      Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                      Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Products", forceLoad: false))" />
    </RadzenStack>

    @* ── Filter bar ──
       Two controls: search box + status filter dropdown. Search is
       server-side (re-runs the query); status filter is client-side
       (operates on the loaded page only). Both reset to page 1 on
       change. *@
    <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1rem;">
        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal"
                     AlignItems="AlignItems.End"
                     JustifyContent="JustifyContent.SpaceBetween"
                     Wrap="FlexWrap.Wrap"
                     Gap="1rem">
            @* Search box — fires OnSearchChanged on Enter or blur.
               `@bind-Value` with the default binding event (onchange) updates
               `_searchTerm` when the user presses Enter or leaves the field.
               `@bind-Value:after` then fires our handler AFTER the value is
               updated, so the handler sees the new value. Same pattern as
               Products.razor. *@
            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["SearchLabel"]" Style="flex: 1 1 240px; min-width: 200px;">
                <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_searchTerm"
                               @bind-Value:after="OnSearchChanged"
                               Placeholder="@Loc["SearchPlaceholder"]"
                               TValue="string" />
            </RadzenFormField>

            @* Status filter dropdown — client-side filter on the loaded page.
               Three+ options: All / Draft / Pending / Approved / Invoiced /
               Cancelled. Labels are localized at render time. *@
            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["StatusLabel"]" Style="flex: 0 1 220px; min-width: 180px;">
                <RadzenDropDown Value="_statusFilter"
                                Data="_statusFilterOptions"
                                TValue="StatusFilter"
                                TextProperty="Label"
                                ValueProperty="Value"
                                ValueChanged="@OnStatusFilterChanged"
                                Style="width: 100%;" />
            </RadzenFormField>
        </RadzenStack>
    </RadzenCard>

    @* ── Loading spinner ── *@
    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <RadzenStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" JustifyContent="JustifyContent.Center"
                     Style="height: 40vh;" Gap="1rem">
            <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false"
                                       Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate"
                                       Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Large" />
            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["Loading"]"
                        TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);" />
        </RadzenStack>
    }

    @* ── Error banner ── *@
    else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_loadError))
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_loadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true">
            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RetryButton"]"
                          Icon="refresh"
                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                          Click="@LoadSalesAsync"
                          Style="margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
        </RadzenAlert>
    }

    @* ── Empty state ──
       Two flavors: no sales at all yet (fresh customer) vs. no sales match
       the current filters. The hint differs slightly to point the user at
       the right next action. *@
    else if (_sales.Count == 0)
    {
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 3rem; text-align: center;">
            <RadzenStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="1rem">
                <RadzenIcon Icon="@(_hasFilters ? "filter_alt_off" : "receipt_long")"
                            Style="font-size: 3rem; color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);" />
                <RadzenText Text="@(_hasFilters ? Loc["EmptyFilteredTitle"] : Loc["EmptyTitle"])"
                            TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" />
                <RadzenText Text="@(_hasFilters ? Loc["EmptyFilteredMessage"] : Loc["EmptyMessage"])"
                            Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); max-width: 360px;" />

                @if (_hasFilters)
                {
                    <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ClearFiltersButton"]"
                                  Icon="filter_alt_off"
                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                                  Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                  Click="@ClearFilters" />
                }
                else
                {
                    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" Gap="0.5rem" Wrap="FlexWrap.Wrap" JustifyContent="JustifyContent.Center">
                        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["GoToCartButton"]"
                                      Icon="shopping_cart"
                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                      Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Cart", forceLoad: false))" />
                        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["BrowseProductsButton"]"
                                      Icon="inventory_2"
                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                                      Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                      Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Products", forceLoad: false))" />
                    </RadzenStack>
                }
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Sales table ──
       RadzenDataGrid with AllowPaging=false (we use the manual pager below
       so server-side pagination drives the page count). AllowSorting=false
       to avoid confusion (sorting client-side on a single page while the
       server has its own DESC ordering would be misleading). *@
    else
    {
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 0.5rem;">
            <RadzenDataGrid Data="@_sales"
                            AllowSorting="false"
                            AllowPaging="false"
                            AllowColumnResize="true"
                            Style="width: 100%;">
                <Columns>
                    @* Sale number — clickable link to /Sales/{Id}. Monospace
                       font + primary color so it reads as an identifier. *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="SaleListItemDto"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColSaleNumber"]"
                                          Width="180px">
                        <Template Context="sale">
                            <RadzenLink Text="@sale.SaleNumber"
                                        Path="@($"/Sales/{sale.Id}")"
                                        class="sale-number-link" />
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* Status — color-coded RadzenBadge. Mapping is in
                       GetStatusBadgeStyle() in the @code block. The label
                       is localized via Loc[$"Status_{sale.Status}"]. *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="SaleListItemDto"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColStatus"]"
                                          Width="140px">
                        <Template Context="sale">
                            <RadzenBadge Text="@GetStatusLabel(sale.Status)"
                                         BadgeStyle="@GetStatusBadgeStyle(sale.Status)"
                                         IsPill="true"
                                         class="sale-status-badge" />
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* Total — right-aligned tabular-numeric. *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="SaleListItemDto"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColTotal"]"
                                          Width="140px"
                                          TextAlign="TextAlign.Right">
                        <Template Context="sale">
                            <span class="sale-total">@FormatMoney(sale.Total)</span>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* Customer name — staff-only. For a customer browsing
                       their own orders this column would be themselves on
                       every row, which is noise. Hiding it for non-staff
                       keeps the table compact on mobile. *@
                    <AuthorizeView Roles="@(Roles.Admin + "," + Roles.Manager + "," + Roles.Employee + "," + Roles.ReadOnly)">
                        <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="SaleListItemDto"
                                              Title="@Loc["ColCustomer"]"
                                              Width="*">
                            <Template Context="sale">
                                <RadzenText Text="@sale.CustomerName" Style="font-weight: 500;" />
                            </Template>
                        </RadzenDataGridColumn>
                    </AuthorizeView>

                    @* Created by — staff-only audit column. Shows which
                       staff member keyed the sale in (often the customer
                       themselves for self-service sales, but could be an
                       employee acting on behalf of a customer). *@
                    <AuthorizeView Roles="@(Roles.Admin + "," + Roles.Manager + "," + Roles.Employee + "," + Roles.ReadOnly)">
                        <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="SaleListItemDto"
                                              Title="@Loc["ColCreatedBy"]"
                                              Width="*">
                            <Template Context="sale">
                                <RadzenText Text="@sale.CreatedByName"
                                            Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);" />
                            </Template>
                        </RadzenDataGridColumn>
                    </AuthorizeView>

                    @* Created at — formatted as date + time in the current
                       culture. Persian culture shows Persian digits + the
                       Jalali (Persian) calendar date when the culture's
                       DateTimeFormatInfo.Calendar is the PersianCalendar;
                       English shows Gregorian. *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="SaleListItemDto"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColCreated"]"
                                          Width="180px">
                        <Template Context="sale">
                            <span class="sale-timestamp">
                                @sale.CreatedAtUtc.LocalDateTime.ToString("g", CultureInfo.CurrentCulture)
                            </span>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    @* Actions — View icon button. Same target as the sale
                       number link, but provides a clearer touch target on
                       mobile. *@
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="SaleListItemDto"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColActions"]"
                                          Width="80px"
                                          TextAlign="TextAlign.Center"
                                          Sortable="false">
                        <Template Context="sale">
                            <RadzenButton Icon="visibility"
                                          Text="@Loc["ViewButton"]"
                                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                          Variant="Variant.Text"
                                          Click="@(() => GoToSaleDetail(sale.Id))" />
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>
                </Columns>
            </RadzenDataGrid>
        </RadzenCard>

        @* ── Pager ──
           Manual pager (Prev / page numbers / Next) — same approach as
           Products.razor. Operates on the PaginatedResult metadata from
           the backend (true server-side paging). The pager is hidden when
           all sales fit on a single page (totalCount <= pageSize). *@
        @if (_totalCount > _pageSize)
        {
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal"
                         JustifyContent="JustifyContent.Center"
                         AlignItems="AlignItems.Center"
                         Gap="0.5rem"
                         Wrap="FlexWrap.Wrap"
                         Style="margin-top: 1rem;">
                <RadzenButton Icon="chevron_left"
                              Variant="Variant.Text"
                              Disabled="@(_pageNumber <= 1)"
                              Click="@(() => OnPageChanged(_pageNumber - 1))" />

                @{
                    var totalPages = (int)Math.Ceiling((double)_totalCount / _pageSize);
                    var startPage = Math.Max(1, _pageNumber - 2);
                    var endPage = Math.Min(totalPages, startPage + 4);
                    if (endPage - startPage < 4) startPage = Math.Max(1, endPage - 4);
                }

                @for (var p = startPage; p <= endPage; p++)
                {
                    var page = p; // closure capture for the lambda
                    <RadzenButton Text="@(page.ToString())"
                                  Variant="@(page == _pageNumber ? Variant.Filled : Variant.Text)"
                                  ButtonStyle="@(page == _pageNumber ? ButtonStyle.Primary : ButtonStyle.Base)"
                                  Disabled="@(_isLoading)"
                                  Click="@(() => OnPageChanged(page))" />
                }

                <RadzenButton Icon="chevron_right"
                              Variant="Variant.Text"
                              Disabled="@(_pageNumber >= Math.Ceiling((double)_totalCount / _pageSize))"
                              Click="@(() => OnPageChanged(_pageNumber + 1))" />

                <RadzenText Text="@string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["PageInfoFormat"], _pageNumber, totalPages, _totalCount)"
                            TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                            Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin-left: 0.5rem;" />
            </RadzenStack>
        }
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── State ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// The page of sales returned by the backend. As of Phase 7 item E,
    /// the status filter is SERVER-SIDE — the query passes the selected
    /// <see cref="SaleStatus"/> into the spec, which becomes part of the
    /// SQL WHERE clause. So this list is already filtered; no client-side
    /// projection needed.
    /// </summary>
    private List<SaleListItemDto> _sales = new();

    /// <summary>
    /// True when the user has entered a search term OR selected a status
    /// filter. Drives the empty-state copy ("no sales at all" vs. "no sales
    /// match your filters") and the empty-state CTA ("Go to cart" vs.
    /// "Clear filters").
    /// </summary>
    private bool _hasFilters =>
        !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_searchTerm) || _statusFilter != StatusFilter.All;

    /// <summary>
    /// Filter state. All start empty/null (= "show everything").
    /// </summary>
    private string _searchTerm = string.Empty;
    private StatusFilter _statusFilter = StatusFilter.All;

    /// <summary>
    /// Pager state. _pageSize=10 matches AdminProducts.razor and keeps the
    /// table on a single screen for typical customers (who rarely have
    /// more than a handful of orders).
    /// </summary>
    private const int _pageSize = 10;
    private int _pageNumber = 1;
    private int _totalCount;

    /// <summary>
    /// Loading/error state.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isLoading = true;
    private string _loadError = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// The dropdown options for the status filter. Built once on init.
    /// Each entry is (Value, Label) — the Label is localized at build time
    /// so the dropdown reflects the current culture. (Re-running
    /// OnInitializedAsync on culture switch rebuilds the labels.)
    /// </summary>
    private List<StatusFilterOption> _statusFilterOptions = new();

    /// <summary>
    /// Simple DTO for the dropdown options. Using a class (not a tuple)
    /// because RadzenDropDown's TextProperty/ValueProperty use reflection.
    /// </summary>
    private sealed class StatusFilterOption
    {
        public StatusFilter Value { get; init; }
        public string Label { get; init; } = string.Empty;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The status filter values. The string values match the SaleStatus
    /// enum's ToString() output so we can compare directly against
    /// SaleListItemDto.Status. Keep these in sync with
    /// TakOne.Domain.Sales.Enums.SaleStatus.
    /// </summary>
    private enum StatusFilter
    {
        All,
        Draft,
        Pending,
        Approved,
        Invoiced,
        Cancelled
    }

    // ── Lifecycle ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Build the status-filter dropdown options. The labels are localized
        // at this point — they won't update if the user switches language
        // mid-session, but the culture switch force-loads the page, which
        // re-runs OnInitializedAsync anyway.
        _statusFilterOptions = new List<StatusFilterOption>
        {
            new() { Value = StatusFilter.All, Label = Loc["StatusAll"] },
            new() { Value = StatusFilter.Draft, Label = Loc["StatusDraft"] },
            new() { Value = StatusFilter.Pending, Label = Loc["StatusPending"] },
            new() { Value = StatusFilter.Approved, Label = Loc["StatusApproved"] },
            new() { Value = StatusFilter.Invoiced, Label = Loc["StatusInvoiced"] },
            new() { Value = StatusFilter.Cancelled, Label = Loc["StatusCancelled"] }
        };

        try
        {
            await LoadSalesAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Data loading ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadSalesAsync()
    {
        _isLoading = true;
        _loadError = string.Empty;

        try
        {
            var query = new GetSalesPaginatedQuery
            {
                PageNumber = _pageNumber,
                PageSize = _pageSize,
                SearchTerm = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_searchTerm) ? null : _searchTerm.Trim(),
                // Map the UI's StatusFilter enum to the domain SaleStatus enum.
                // StatusFilter.All → null (no filter). The other values line up
                // 1:1 with SaleStatus by name. This mapping is checked at compile
                // time by the switch expression — adding a new SaleStatus without
                // adding it here would surface as a compiler warning.
                Status = _statusFilter switch
                {
                    StatusFilter.All => null,
                    StatusFilter.Draft => SaleStatus.Draft,
                    StatusFilter.Pending => SaleStatus.Pending,
                    StatusFilter.Approved => SaleStatus.Approved,
                    StatusFilter.Invoiced => SaleStatus.Invoiced,
                    StatusFilter.Cancelled => SaleStatus.Cancelled,
                    _ => null
                }
            };

            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<PaginatedResult<SaleListItemDto>>(query);

            _sales = result.Items.ToList();
            _totalCount = result.TotalCount;

            // If the page is now empty (e.g. user filtered down to nothing),
            // bump the page number back to 1 and retry. Common case: user
            // was on page 5, then applied a filter that only has 2 pages —
            // we don't want to leave them stranded on an empty page 5.
            if (_sales.Count == 0 && _pageNumber > 1)
            {
                _pageNumber = 1;
                await LoadSalesAsync();
                return;
            }
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            _loadError = Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Filter change handlers ──────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task OnSearchChanged()
    {
        // `_searchTerm` has already been updated by @bind-Value before this
        // handler fires (that's what :after means). Reset the page and re-load.
        _pageNumber = 1;
        await LoadSalesAsync();
    }

    private async Task OnStatusFilterChanged(StatusFilter filter)
    {
        // Status filter is SERVER-SIDE (Phase 7 item E) — the filter value
        // is pushed into the GetSalesPaginatedQuery.Status field, which
        // becomes a SQL WHERE clause via the spec. So changing the filter
        // requires a backend reload. We also reset to page 1 because the
        // previous page number may be out of range for the filtered set.
        _statusFilter = filter;
        _pageNumber = 1;
        await LoadSalesAsync();
    }

    private async Task OnPageChanged(int newPage)
    {
        _pageNumber = newPage;
        await LoadSalesAsync();
    }

    private async Task ClearFilters()
    {
        _searchTerm = string.Empty;
        _statusFilter = StatusFilter.All;
        _pageNumber = 1;
        await LoadSalesAsync();
    }

    // ── Navigation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private void GoToSaleDetail(Guid saleId)
    {
        // Phase 4.3 will build /Sales/{Id}. For now, navigating there will
        // 404 — but the route is reserved and the URL is meaningful (users
        // can copy/paste it). Once 4.3 lands, this just works.
        Navigation.NavigateTo($"/Sales/{saleId}", forceLoad: false);
    }

    // ── Display helpers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Formats a MoneyDto for display: amount in current culture + currency
    /// code. Persian culture shows Persian digits + RTL; English shows
    /// Latin digits + LTR. The currency code is shown as-is (e.g. "IRR"
    /// or "USD") — same convention as Products.razor and Cart.razor.
    /// </summary>
    private static string FormatMoney(MoneyDto? money)
    {
        if (money is null) return "—";
        return $"{money.Amount.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.CurrentCulture)} {money.Currency}";
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Maps a sale status string (the SaleStatus enum's ToString() output)
    /// to a Radzen BadgeStyle for color coding:
    ///   - Draft     → Base      (gray, "in progress, not yet submitted")
    ///   - Pending   → Warning   (amber, "awaiting approval")
    ///   - Approved  → Info      (blue, "approved, ready to invoice")
    ///   - Invoiced  → Success   (green, "complete")
    ///   - Cancelled → Danger    (red, "cancelled")
    /// 
    /// Unknown status strings (defensive: shouldn't happen unless the enum
    /// gains a new value without updating this mapping) fall back to Base.
    /// </summary>
    private static BadgeStyle GetStatusBadgeStyle(string status) => status switch
    {
        "Draft" => BadgeStyle.Base,
        "Pending" => BadgeStyle.Warning,
        "Approved" => BadgeStyle.Info,
        "Invoiced" => BadgeStyle.Success,
        "Cancelled" => BadgeStyle.Danger,
        _ => BadgeStyle.Base
    };

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns a localized label for the sale status. Falls back to the
    /// raw status string if no localization key matches (defensive —
    /// shouldn't happen unless the enum gains a new value).
    /// </summary>
    private string GetStatusLabel(string status)
    {
        var key = $"Status{status}";
        var localized = Loc[key];
        // If the localizer can't find the key, it returns the key itself.
        // In that case, fall back to the raw status string.
        return localized == key ? status : localized;
    }
}